&lt;p&gt;We’re seeking AI &amp;amp; People Transformation Interns to help reimagine how our People teams work. You’ll examine how process design, data, and emerging AI tools can help simplify and improve everyday experiences for employees, managers, recruiters, and People team partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based in our New York City office and working within the People PMO, you’ll partner with mentors, project leaders, People teams, and IT to map operational workflows, identify friction points and opportunities for AI or automation, and help assess or test practical solutions. We’re looking for interns who bring a fresh perspective, look for opportunities to rethink existing workflows, and connect ideas across projects. The work is transformation-focused: looking beyond existing processes to redesign work thoughtfully and build improvements that can scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for in you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In the process of receiving a Bachelor’s or Master&#39;s degree in business, management, operations, information systems, or business analytics; we welcome other backgrounds that demonstrate an interest in operational improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have hands-on exposure to AI tools and curiosity about how to use them effectively in practical workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly, work collaboratively, and bring curiosity, sound judgment, and eagerness to learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can research a process or question, synthesize what you learn, document it clearly, and approach problems in a structured way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re organized, attentive to detail, curious about employee or candidate experience, and motivated to make processes simpler.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a minimum of one quarter/semester remaining in university studies after the internship concludes. Graduation date in Fall 2027 or Spring 2028.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be authorized to work in the United States.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll find at MongoDB&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Authentic Culture: A workplace where you are encouraged to bring your whole self to work, we believe that Embracing the Power of Differences is the best way to broaden our own perspectives and foster innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personalized Mentorship: Pair up with a team Mentor, a Program Advisor from the Early Talent Recruitment Team, and an &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/careers/diversity-and-inclusion&quot;&gt;Employee Resource Group&lt;/a&gt; (ERG) Guide to foster your growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career Coaching Sessions: Access to a tailored training program designed uniquely for interns’ personal and professional development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work-Life Harmony: Embrace &quot;Bloom for Interns&quot; with access to mental and physical health benefits, paid time off, free lunch, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Impactful Projects: Contribute to projects where you can Make it Matter - your meaningful work will see the light of day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exclusive Networking: Attend &quot;Speaker Series&quot; and &quot;Roundtables&quot; to connect with our executives and departmental leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vibrant Community: Build connections with fellow interns and join after-work social events, virtual gatherings, and local city activities to create connections and friendships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relocation Support: Financial assistance, housing, and a commuting stipend to allow you to comfortably settle into your new location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Path to Full-Time: A chance to see if MongoDB is where you see yourself long term with the possibility of receiving a full time offer at the end of the summer!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
